{"id":"resp_bd6d5dd2cc0d820f","created_at":1795617935,"incomplete_details":null,"instructions":null,"metadata":null,"model":"gpt-oss-120b","object":"response","output":[{"id":"rs_879aa21d5da10e88","summary":[],"type":"reasoning","content":[{"text":"We need to assess SHACL candidate against represented requirement. Requirement: IMO-083 clause 9.3.2.1.3: \"When ice accretion is likely, every required navigation or communication antenna must be equipped with means to prevent ice accumulation.\" So need condition: ship with iceAccretionLikely true and hasRequiredNavigationOrCommunicationAntenna ?antenna, and antenna must have antennaIceAccumulationPreventionPresent true (or iceAccumulationPreventionMeansPresent?). The candidate uses property antennaIceAccumulationPreventionPresent true, okay.\n\nCheck mapping: evidence shows requiredNavigationOrCommunicationAntenna property is datatype XSD:string but in representation they treat it as object property linking ship to antenna. In schema E112 defines datatype property but Vocab says it's datatype property. However in representation they use it as object property linking ship to antenna (hasRequiredNavigationOrCommunicationAntenna is object property). But requirement uses requiredNavigationOrCommunicationAntenna (maybe as dataprop). There is also hasRequiredNavigationOrCommunicationAntenna (object property). The candidate uses hasRequiredNavigationOrCommunicationAntenna, not requiredNavigationOrCommunicationAntenna. In representation evidence E88 says hasRequiredNavigationOrCommunicationAntenna domain ship, range navigationOrCommunicationAntenna, object property. But requirement says \"required navigation or communication antenna\". That maps to property requiredNavigationOrCommunicationAntenna (datatype), but semantic meaning is linking via hasRequired... So possible mismatch: need to use proper property consistent with representation. The model paths (E151) says owners: iceAccretionLikely and hasRequiredNavigationOrCommunicationAntenna are on ship, antennaIceAccumulationPreventionPresent on antenna. So candidate matches.\n\nPotential missing constraints: need to ensure that antennaIceAccumulationPreventionPresent is boolean true, but schema defines datatype boolean, fine. However need also check that antenna is of type navigationOrCommunicationAntenna (E122 class). The query doesn't restrict ?antenna type, but could be any node linked. Might be okay but could be missing type check.\n\nAlso requirement: \"every required navigation or communication antenna\". Should ensure for each antenna linked via hasRequiredNavigationOrCommunicationAntenna, the prevention property true. Candidate uses NOT EXISTS filter, okay.\n\nPotential issue: the message uses “ice‑accumulation‑prevention means” while property is antennaIceAccumulationPreventionPresent. That's fine.\n\nMissing activation? The shape targetClass ship, good.\n\nPotential missing constraint: need to consider the iceAccretionLikely property is boolean literal true. Ensure literal is xsd:boolean. Property defined as datatype boolean (E25). OK.\n\nPotential gap: The requirement also mentions \"means to prevent ice accumulation\" could be represented by either antennaIceAccumulationPreventionPresent or iceAccumulationPreventionMeansPresent (different property). The schema includes both but mapping says antennaIceAccumulationPreventionPresent is the appropriate for each antenna. So fine.\n\nThus candidate appears correct. No defects. No unresolved questions. So assessment APPROVE.\n\nNeed to output JSON with assessment APPROVE, empty issues and questions arrays.\n\nCheck max_issues 12 okay.\n\nReturn object.\n\n","type":"reasoning_text"}],"encrypted_content":null,"status":null},{"id":"msg_a2828276620c84f5","content":[{"annotations":[],"text":"{\n  \"assessment\": \"APPROVE\",\n  \"issues\": [],\n  \"questions\": []\n}","type":"output_text","logprobs":null}],"role":"assistant","status":"completed","type":"message","phase":null}],"parallel